# Netlify _headers file
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Place this file (named exactly "_headers", no extension) in the same
# publish folder as index.html. Netlify reads it automatically on deploy —
# no netlify.toml or build step needed.
#
# Forces browsers (and Netlify's own CDN) to always revalidate these files
# with the origin server before trusting any cached copy, instead of
# serving a stale version silently. Without this, the browser's normal
# HTTP cache can keep serving an old sw.js/index.html even though the
# service worker's own cache logic is correctly set to network-first —
# the request never reaches the network layer at all if the HTTP cache
# intercepts it first. This was almost certainly why "redeployed and
# nothing changed" kept happening.

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/manifest.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
